# Tier 1 adaptation for the Zinwa Q25 (MT6789 / Helio G99, 3.5" 720x720).
#
# Only what cannot be derived belongs here. Vendor API level, panel geometry
# and the touchscreen node all derive correctly on a Treble device; what
# follows is the square panel - whose usable numbers are a layout judgement,
# not a measurement - and the key devices, which derivation cannot separate on
# this hardware.

# The power key and the volume rocker, pinned by name.
#
# Derivation takes everything claiming KEY_POWER or a volume key that is not
# the touchscreen, and on the Q25 that over-collects badly: the keyboard is one
# input device carrying the whole QWERTY *and* the toolbelt keys *and* the
# trackpad (drivers/input/keyboard/bbqX0kbd registers EV_KEY, EV_REL and
# BTN_LEFT/RIGHT on the single "Q25_keyboard" node), so it claims volume keys
# on its Sym layer and would be treated as a key device.
#
# These two are the real ones, read from the device's own kernel sources:
# drivers/input/keyboard/mtk-pmic-keys.c sets input_dev->name =
# "mtk-pmic-keys" (the PMIC power key) and mtk-kpd.c registers the matrix
# keypad the volume rocker hangs off. Pinned by name, never by node number -
# numbering here depends on probe order across ~160 vendor modules.
#
# UNVERIFIED: mtk-kpd.c takes its name from KPD_NAME, which is defined in a
# header this port has not read. If the journal logs that "mtk-kpd" did not
# resolve, get the right string from
#   grep -h '^N: Name' /proc/bus/input/devices
# and correct it here.
deviceinfo_key_devices_by_name="mtk-pmic-keys;mtk-kpd"

# 3.5" diagonal, 720x720: sqrt(720^2 + 720^2) / 3.5 = 291 ppi.
#
# GridUnit = round(dpi * 1.44 / 25.4) = 16, which is 1.40 mm of glass per grid
# unit against sargo's 1.44 mm - i.e. the shell chrome comes out the same
# physical size as on a device where it is known to fit. In grid units the
# screen is 720/16 = 45 wide against sargo's 43, so the fixed-size system menu
# (Units.gu(40) = 640 px) fits the 720 px width with margin.
#
# For contrast, LineageOS ships TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY := 193 on this device,
# which would give GridUnit 11 - a third smaller than sargo in physical terms.
# That is a reasonable choice for Android's scrolling lists and a poor one for
# webOS's fixed chrome, so it is recorded here rather than copied.
#
# UNVERIFIED ON HARDWARE. sargo needed a device pixel ratio well away from its
# natural one; expect to re-tune both of these.
deviceinfo_display_dpi="291"

# webOS apps are fixed-layout Enyo pages, so the ratio decides how many CSS
# pixels they are handed. 720 / 1.6 = 450, exactly the canvas width sargo
# targets (1080 / 2.4) and what the pages are built for.
#
# The height is the part with no good answer: 450 CSS px tall as well, against
# the ~1000 a portrait phone gives. Pages that scroll are fine; pages with a
# fixed footer will be tight. If that proves worse than small text, 1.875
# (= 384 CSS px square) trades width for headroom.
deviceinfo_device_pixel_ratio="1.6"

# Deliberately absent:
#
#   deviceinfo_video_call
#       The 8 MP front camera is real and the MediaTek camera HAL enumerates
#       it; leave derivation to decide once it has been shown to deliver
#       frames. mindphone is the precedent for closing this off when the
#       cameras enumerate but do not work.
#
#   deviceinfo_touchscreen_by_name
#       mtk_touchscreen_hodafonehw.ko is the only touch device on the bus, so
#       derivation cannot pick the wrong one.
